\subsubsection{Class Imbalance Handling}

To address the significant class imbalance (73\% pneumonia, 27\% normal), we implemented weighted random sampling during training:

\begin{lstlisting}[language=Python, caption=Weighted Sampling Implementation]
def get_weighted_sampler(dataset):
    labels = np.array(dataset.labels)
    class_counts = np.bincount(labels)
    class_weights = 1.0 / (class_counts + 1e-8)
    sample_weights = class_weights[labels]
    
    return WeightedRandomSampler(
        weights=torch.DoubleTensor(sample_weights),
        num_samples=len(sample_weights),
        replacement=True
    )
\end{lstlisting}

The implementation works as follows:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Extract all class labels from the dataset.
    \item Count the number of samples in each class using \text{np.bincount}.
    \item Compute inverse class frequencies to assign higher weights to underrepresented classes.
    \item Map these weights to each sample to generate \text{sample\_weights}.
    \item Use \text{WeightedRandomSampler} to sample data points such that minority classes are more likely to be selected.
\end{itemize}


